Package: mosd
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: mos build <mos@example.invalid>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: default-dbus-system-bus | dbus-system-bus, mos-profile, mos-system (= @VERSION@), ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: mos management daemon
 Owns the com.mos.mosd D-Bus interface: the settings tree, device health,
 power actions and update state. Ships the root-only bus policy for that name
 alongside the binary, so the daemon's access boundary travels with it.
 .
 The package owns its enablement: mosd.service and the
 multi-user.target.wants symlink that starts it are both payload, so
 installing this package is what makes the daemon run.
